      "title": "Content",
      "content": [
        "# MD-JSON Two-Way Sync System\r",
        "\r",
        "This system provides bidirectional synchronization between Markdown files and JSON files optimized for AI consumption.\r",
        "\r",
        "## Features\r",
        "\r",
        "- **Two-Way Synchronization**: Changes in either format automatically update the other\r",
        "- **Real-time Watching**: Continuously monitors for changes in both file types\r",
        "- **Multiple Conflict Resolution Methods**: Choose how to handle conflicts between formats\r",
        "- **Automatic Background Operation**: Can run silently at Windows startup\r",
        "- **Structured JSON Format**: Optimized for AI consumption and reduced token usage\r",
        "\r",
        "## Components\r",
        "\r",
        "- **md-json-sync.js** - Core Node.js script providing bidirectional synchronization\r",
        "- **md-json-sync.bat** - Windows batch script for running the synchronizer\r",
        "- **start-md-json-sync-watcher.bat** - Script to start the watcher in background\r",
        "- **start-md-json-sync-silent.vbs** - Silent runner for Windows Task Scheduler\r",
        "- **setup-md-json-sync-startup.bat** - Sets up automatic startup\r",
        "- **remove-md-json-sync-startup.bat** - Removes the startup task\r",
        "\r",
        "## Basic Usage\r",
        "\r",
        "### One-time Synchronization\r",
        "```\r",
        "md-json-sync.bat\r",
        "```\r",
        "\r",
        "### Watch Mode (Manual)\r",
        "```\r",
        "md-json-sync.bat --watch\r",
        "```\r",
        "\r",
        "### Watch Mode with Verbose Output\r",
        "```\r",
        "md-json-sync.bat --watch --verbose\r",
        "```\r",
        "\r",
        "### Background Watch Mode\r",
        "```\r",
        "start-md-json-sync-watcher.bat\r",
        "```\r",
        "\r",
        "## Conflict Resolution\r",
        "\r",
        "When both the Markdown and JSON versions of a file have been modified, the system needs to determine which version to consider authoritative. You can specify a conflict resolution method:\r",
        "\r",
        "- **Timestamp-based (default)**: The most recently modified file wins\r",
        "- **Prefer Markdown**: Always use Markdown as the source of truth\r",
        "- **Prefer JSON**: Always use JSON as the source of truth\r",
        "\r",
        "```\r",
        "md-json-sync.bat --watch --prefer-md\r",
        "```\r",
        "\r",
        "## Automatic Startup\r",
        "\r",
        "To configure the two-way sync watcher to start automatically when Windows starts:\r",
        "\r",
        "1. Right-click **setup-md-json-sync-startup.bat**\r",
        "2. Select **Run as administrator**\r",
        "3. Follow the prompts\r",
        "\r",
        "This will create a Windows Task Scheduler task that runs the watcher on login.\r",
        "\r",
        "## Remove Automatic Startup\r",
        "\r",
        "To remove the automatic startup configuration:\r",
        "\r",
        "1. Right-click **remove-md-json-sync-startup.bat**\r",
        "2. Select **Run as administrator**\r",
        "3. Follow the prompts\r",
        "\r",
        "## Checking Status\r",
        "\r",
        "To check if the watcher is currently running:\r",
        "\r",
        "1. Open Task Manager\r",
        "2. Look for **cmd.exe** processes\r",
        "3. One of them should show \"MD-JSON Two-Way Sync\" in the command line\r",
        "\r",
        "## Troubleshooting\r",
        "\r",
        "If the watcher is not working correctly:\r",
        "\r",
        "1. Check that Node.js is installed and in your PATH\r",
        "2. Try running `md-json-sync.bat --verbose` to see detailed output\r",
        "3. Check for error messages in the command window\r",
        "4. Verify the directories in the config section of md-json-sync.js\r",
        "\r",
        "## Manually Stopping the Watcher\r",
        "\r",
        "To stop the watcher process:\r",
        "\r",
        "1. Open Task Manager\r",
        "2. Find the CMD window with \"MD-JSON Two-Way Sync\" in the command line\r",
        "3. Select it and click \"End task\"\r",
        "\r",
        "## File Organization\r",
        "\r",
        "For each Markdown file, the corresponding JSON file is stored in a \"json\" subdirectory within the same directory:\r",
        "\r",
        "- `shortlinks/cfish.md` ↔ `shortlinks/json/cfish.json`\r",
        "- `docs/glossary.md` ↔ `docs/json/glossary.json`\r",
        "\r",
        "This bidirectional relationship means you can edit either file, and the other will be automatically updated to match.\r",
        "\r",
        "## More Information\r",
        "\r",
        "For more details about the MD-JSON sync system, see:\r",
        "- [JSON Sync System Documentation](./docs/json-sync-system.md)\r",
        "\r",
        "## Current Status\r",
        "\r",
        "The MD-JSON Two-Way Sync System is now fully operational with the following status:\r",
        "\r",
        "- ✅ Markdown-to-JSON synchronization: Working correctly\r",
        "- ✅ JSON-to-Markdown synchronization: Fixed and working correctly\r",
        "- ✅ File monitoring for Markdown changes: Working correctly\r",
        "- ✅ File monitoring for JSON changes: Fixed and working correctly\r",
        "- ✅ Conflict resolution strategies: Implemented and tested\r",
        "- ✅ Windows Task Scheduler automation: Working correctly\r",
        "\r",
        "## Testing\r",
        "\r",
        "To test the system's bidirectional capabilities:\r",
        "\r",
        "1. Start the watcher: `md-json-sync.bat --watch --verbose`\r",
        "2. Edit a Markdown file and save it - observe the JSON file being updated\r",
        "3. Edit the corresponding JSON file and save it - observe the Markdown file being updated\r",
        "\r",
        "You can also use the test script to verify the JSON-to-Markdown conversion:\r",
        "\r",
        "```\r",
        "node test-json-to-md.js\r",
        "```\r",
        "\r",
        "This script reads `docs/json/sync-test.json` and generates `docs/sync-test-from-json.md` to demonstrate the conversion process.\r",
        "\r",
        "## Recent Improvements\r",
        "\r",
        "The following issues have been fixed in the latest update:\r",
        "\r",
        "1. Fixed JSON-to-Markdown synchronization by correcting file path handling\r",
        "2. Improved file monitoring for JSON changes with dedicated watchers\r",
        "3. Enhanced error handling and directory management\r",
        "4. Fixed path resolution for complex directory structures\r",
        "5. Added better feedback in verbose mode\r",
        "\r",
        "## Future Improvements\r",
        "\r",
        "Planned improvements for future versions:\r",
        "\r",
        "1. Add more robust error recovery mechanisms\r",
        "2. Implement bidirectional conflict resolution with user prompts\r",
        "3. Add a graphical user interface for monitoring sync status\r",
        "4. Improve performance for large file sets\r",
        "5. Add support for custom file extensions and directories"
      ]
    }
  ],
